mers.\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- The sources give only growth rates. They give no absolute capex figures, so I can't state a total C$ need for 2027.\n\n**Funding gap that can be identified:**\n- Pellham had planned a C$2.4B equity offering and withdrew it after investor demand fell short (pellham-offering). That C$2.4B is the clearest sized external gap in the sources.\n- Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (utility-credit), so it appears able to fund through debt.\n- No source gives cash flow from operations, dividends or total debt capacity, so I can't compute a sector-wide gap.\n\n**Market conditions (utility-credit):**\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, but the debt market is still open.\n- Equity is weaker: two utility share offerings were cut back in size, and Pellham's was pulled.\n\n**What this implies:**\n- The gap shows up mainly as unfunded equity, around C$2.4B at Pellham. Bonds can fill only part of it, and only at wider spreads.\n- Pellham is adjusting its plan rather than closing the gap. It will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves.\n- The effective 2027 capex that will actually be spent is therefore below the stated plan for Pellham. Norvane's plan looks more likely to go ahead.","ttft_ms":2648,"type":"result","duration_ms":21712,"uuid":"de31dfeb-6e8c-414d-a457-47d2e71a292d","ttft_stream_ms":1701,"time_to_request_ms":155,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":12,"input_attachments":30,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":17,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":5,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":5,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"